sensor-bme680 (2.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild against libwildlifesystems 1.3.0, so "{{node}}" in a sensor's
    location resolves to the node's own coordinates from /etc/geolocation
    instead of being emitted as an unresolved token
  * Require libwildlifesystems-dev (>= 1.3.0). The library is static, so the
    behaviour above is fixed at build time: a binary built against 1.2.0 would
    satisfy the old pin and silently emit unresolved tokens under the same
    package version

 -- Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0100

sensor-bme680 (2.2.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Zero-initialise default_config. It sets every field explicitly except
    location, which was left reading uninitialised stack memory on nodes with
    no config file; a garbage source of WS_LOC_EXPLICIT would have emitted a
    GeoJSON Point built from uninitialised coordinates

 -- Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0100

sensor-bme680 (2.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Report device "bme680" and the sensor's configured location
  * Support "location" in /etc/ws/sensors/bme680.json
  * Use ws_json_object_end for config object bounds, so a config entry may
    contain nested objects
  * Rebuild against libwildlifesystems 1.2.0
  * Declare libwildlifesystems-dev (>= 1.2.0) in Build-Depends and
    sensor-control (>= 1.3.0) in Depends. Neither was declared at all,
    though the binary links -lwildlifesystems and runs sc-prototype

 -- Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0100

